          %blockquote
            %p
              the following are rough unpolished notes taken more or less verbatim from some seminar talk – needs attention, meaning:
              %strong somebody should go through this and polish
          %hr/
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#preorientations_of_"}
                  Preorientations of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
              %li
                %a{:href => "#orientations_of_"}
                  Orientations of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
              %li
                %a{:href => "#connection_to_complex_orientation"} Connection to complex orientation
          %h1#introduction Introduction
          %p
            Recall from last time that given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            an algebraic group such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+spectrum"} formal spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spf
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spf A(\mathbb{C}P^\infty)
            is the completion
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℴ
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{S^1}({*}) := \mathcal{o}_{G}
            then passing to germs gave a completion map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %mi Bor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A_{S^1}({*}) \to A(\mathbb{C}P^\infty) =
                  A^{Bor}_{S^1}({*}).
          %p The problem we (begin) to address here is how to extend this equivariant cohomology to other spaces besides the point. This requires derived algebraic geometry.
          %h1#derived_group_schemes Derived group schemes
          %p
            Recall that a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
            over a scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G: \mathrm{Sch} /X^{op} \to \mathrm{Ab}
          %p
            such that composition with the forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ab
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: \mathrm{Ab} \to \mathrm{Set}
            is representable.
          %p
            We would like extend this definition to the world of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
          %ol
            %li
              %p Because of the higher categorical nature of derived schemes Hom sets are spaces.
            %li
              %p
                Everything should in the
                = succeed "-setting," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We will not worry about the second concern and address the first by replacing the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Ab}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} TopAb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{TopAb}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Set}
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Top}
          %blockquote
            %p
              The following definition is somewhat restrictive and really should incorporate more of the
              = succeed "-structure." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            %strong Definition
            A commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a topological functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} DSch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} TopAb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G: \mathrm{DSch} / X^{op} \to \mathrm{TopAb}
          %p
            such that composition with the forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} TopAb
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: \mathrm{TopAb} \to \mathrm{Top}
            is representable (up to weak equivalence) by an object which is
            %span.newWikiWord
              flat
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/flat+object"} ?
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            %strong Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                be a scheme, then we have an associated
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{X}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{X}
                is obtained by viewing the structure sheaf of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                as a presheaf of
                = succeed "-rings" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{X}
                and commutative
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
                we have a map from commutative
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to commutative
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 X
          %h1#preorientations Preorientations
          %p
            Throughout
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            will be an
            = succeed "-ring," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the affine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{S^1}
            the
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma (G)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty}
            the
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty} = \mathrm{Hom}_{E_\infty} (\mathbb{C}P^\infty , A).
          %p
            %strong> Definition
            (Preliminary) A preorientation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a morphism of commutative
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spf
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma : \mathrm{Spf} A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty} \to G,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spf
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spf} A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty}
            is the completion wrt the ideal
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                        %msup
                          %mi P
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi pt
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{ker} (A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty} \to A^{pt} = A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spf
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat \sigma : \mathrm{Spf} A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty} \to \hat G
          %p is an isomorphism.
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is affine, then a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spf
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma : \mathrm{Spf} A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty} \to G
          %p
            corresponds to a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{S^1} \to A^{\mathbb{C}P^\infty}
            which is the same as a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{C}P^\infty \to \mathrm{Hom} (X, G) = G(X).
          %p Hence we are led to the following definition.
          %p
            %strong Definition
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a morphism of topological commutative monoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℙ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{P} (\mathbb{C} [\alpha]) = \mathbb{C}P^\infty \to G(X).
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^\infty
            is nearly freely generated. Indeed it follows from the fundamental theorem of algebra that as a topological monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^\infty
            is generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^1
            subject to the single relation that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} pt
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{pt} = \mathbb{C}P^0 \subset \mathbb{C}P^1
            is the monoidal unit.
          %p
            %strong Proposition
            A preorientation up to homotopy is a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \simeq \mathbb{C}P^1 \to G(X)
          %p
            that is an element of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2 (G(X))
          %p
            Hence, we always have at least one preorientation: the trivial one which corresponds to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in \pi_2 (G(X))
          %h1#orientations Orientations
          %p
            As motivation recall that a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s: A \to B
            of 1-dim
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s'
            is invertible. We would like to encode this in our derived language (without defining
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s'
          %p
            %strong Definition
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            = succeed "-ring," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : S^2 \to G(A)
            a preorientation. Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            is an orientation if
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 G \to \mathrm{Spec} \pi_0 A
                is smooth of relative dimension 1, and
            %li
              %p
                The map induced by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo :
                      %mi ω
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : \omega \to \pi_2 A
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mi A
                      %mi ω
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 2
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\pi_n A \otimes_{\pi_0 A} \omega \to \pi_{n+2} A
              %p
                is an isomorphism for each
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Note that (2) implies that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is weakly periodic. Conversely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is weakly periodic then (2) is equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            being an isomorphism.
          %p
            Before defining
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            we extend the above definition to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
          %p
            %strong Definition
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma: S^2 \to G(X)
            a preorientation. Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            is an orientation if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G, \sigma) |_U
            is an orientation for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
            affine.
          %p
            We now define the module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            and the map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            = succeed "-ring," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+group+scheme"} derived group scheme
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0 = \pi_0 G
            a scheme over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \pi_0 A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            denote the sheaf of differentials on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0 / \pi_0 A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega := i^* \Omega, \; i: \mathrm{Spec} \pi_0 A \to G
          %p is the identity section.
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow G
            be an open affine subscheme containing the identity section, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \mathrm{Spec} B
            for some
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            induces a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to A^{S^2}
            which is the same as a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0 B \to A(S^2)= \pi_0 A \oplus \pi_2 A .
          %p
            It is a fact that the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 B \to \pi_2 A
            is a derivation over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 A
            and hence has a classifying map which yields a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi ω
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : \omega \to \pi_2 A .
          %h1#the_multiplicative_derived_group_scheme The Multiplicative Derived Group Scheme
          %p
            The naive guess for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1 (A) = A^x = (\pi_0 A)^x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \mathbf{S}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1 (A)
            an Abelian group as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is rational, that is there is a map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Q} \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1 (A)
            can be given an Abelian group structure. Hence,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1
            is a perfectly good
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
            defined on the category of rational
            = succeed "-rings," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "-rings." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            Recall that for a ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Hom
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^x = \mathrm{Hom}_R (R [ t, t^{-1} ] , R)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            we can form the group algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[M]
            which is really a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} R[M]
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[m]
            is characterized by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ring
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ring
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{Ring} ( R[M] , B) = \mathrm{Ring} (R, B) \times \mathrm{Mon} (M,B)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Mon
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Mon}
            is the category of monoids and the ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is thought of as a monoid wrt to multiplication. Motivated by these observations we make the following definitions.
          %p
            %strong Definition
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            a topological Abelian monoid, then we can define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[M]
            which is characterized by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Alg
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Alg
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} TopMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{Alg}_A (A[M], B) \simeq \mathrm{Alg}_A (A,B) \times \mathrm{TopMon} (M, B^\times ).
          %p
            Recall that because of the higher categorical nature of things, the hom-sets above are spaces and the symbol
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
            indicates weak equivalence of spaces.
          %p
            %strong Definition
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            = succeed "-ring." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_m = \mathrm{Spec} A[ \mathbb{Z}].
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            is a derived commutative group scheme over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A
          %p
            Note that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* ( A[ \mathbb{Z}]) = (\pi_* A) [ \mathbb{Z}]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 G_m \to \pi_0 \mathrm{Spec}  A
            is smooth of relative dimension 1.
          %h2#preorientations_of_
            Preorientations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
          %p
            %strong Proposition
            For any
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            and maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty ] \to A
          %p
            The proof follows from the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            is initial in the category of
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A [ \mathbb{Z}]
          %p
            %strong Corollary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \mathbf{S} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty ]
            is the moduli space of preorientations of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            is defined over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            is the same as a map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A \to \mathrm{Spec} \mathbf{S} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty ]
          %h2#orientations_of_
            Orientations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
          %p
            We consider the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo :
                  %mi ω
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : \omega \to \pi_2 A
            where
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                      %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega = i^* \Omega^1_{\pi_0 G / \pi_0 \mathrm{Spec} A}
          %p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            is the identity section. Note that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 G_m = (\pi_0 A ) [t, t^{-1}]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is canonically trivial, so an orientation is just an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mi σ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_\sigma \in \pi_2 A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi β
                    %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_\sigma
            is invertible in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* A
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            denote the (universal) orientation of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty]
          %p
            %strong Theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi β
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \mathbf{S} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty] [ \beta^{-1}]
            is the moduli space of orientations of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
          %p
            It is a theorem of Snaith, that this moduli space has the homotopy type of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU
            the spectrum of complex K-theory. Note that by considering the homtopy fixed points of a certain action there is a way to recover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KO
            as well.
          %h2#connection_to_complex_orientation Connection to complex orientation
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be an
            = succeed "-ring," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            defines a cohomology theory. An orientation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A
            is a map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KU
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU
            is complex oriented, we see that an orientation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_m
            gives a complex orientation by precomposing with the map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                    %mo →
                    %mi KU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU \to KU
          %h1#the_additive_derived_group_scheme The Additive Derived Group Scheme
          %p
            The naive definition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_a
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1 (A)
            is the additive group of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} \mathbf{S}
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_k \mathbf{A}^1_A = \oplus_{n \ge 0} A^{-k} (B \Sigma_n )
          %p where as if it were flat we would have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_k \mathbf{A}^1_A = \pi_k A [x] .
          %p
            Also,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1
            is not commutative.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1 (A)
            is an infinite loop space, but not an Abelian monoid. Again
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}^1
            is a derived group scheme when restricted to rational
            = succeed "-rings." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %p
            We no restrict to the category of integral
            = succeed "-rings," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z} \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z}
            is initial.
          %p
            %strong Definition
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an integral
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mi a
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G^A_a = \mathrm{Spec} ( A \otimes_\mathbb{Z} \mathbb{Z} [x] ).
          %p
            It can be shown that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mi a
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G^A_a
            is flat and has the correct amount of commutativity.
          %blockquote
            %p
              Why can’t we just use
              = succeed "?" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} A [ \mathbb{N}]
          %p
            %strong Proposition
            For all integral
            = succeed "-rings," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi G
                    %mi a
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_a^A
            are in bijective correspondence with maps
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty] \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} H \mathbb{Z} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty]
            is the moduli space of preorientations of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_a
          %p
            Now,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_* H \mathbb{Z} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty] = H_* (\mathbb{C} P^\infty , \mathbb{Z} )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \in \pi_2 H \mathbb{Z} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty]
          %p
            %strong Proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi β
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} H \mathbb{Z} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty ] [ \beta^{-1}]
            is the moduli space of orientations of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_a
          %p
            %strong Proposition
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi β
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi KU
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Spec} H \mathbb{Z} [ \mathbb{C} P^\infty ] [ \beta^{-1}] = KU \otimes \mathbb{Q}
